Acknowledgement — MARK LIV (JARVIS)
-----------------------------------
ORION's software-rendered avatar, viseme lip-sync, acoustic echo guard and
measured audio-device probing were informed by the approach described in the
MARK LIV release notes by FatihMakes (https://github.com/FatihMakes/Mark-LIV),
which is published under CC BY-NC 4.0.

No code from that project is included here. ORION's implementations were
written independently for this codebase; what was taken is the engineering
*approach* — reading mouth openness and width from formant bands rather than a
volume meter, supplying lip closures from the transcript because no spectrum
reveals them, reducing characters to bare Latin letters so articulation needs
no per-language table, subtracting band energies to tell an assistant's own
voice from a user's, and measuring audio devices instead of trusting their
capability flags. Techniques are not subject to copyright; the acknowledgement
is offered because the ideas were genuinely useful and deserve credit.

